    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Nassau County",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9195\n\nSPONSOR: RHOADS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act authorizing the county of Nassau to alienate and sell parklands\nto Lakeside Inn, Inc.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 authorizes the county of Nassau to discontinue parkland to\nLakeside Inn, Inc. for residential improvements.\n\nSection 2 provides that section I shall only be effective upon the\ncondition that Lakeside Inn, Inc. conveys land designated under section\n4 to the county of Nassau.\n\nSection 3 outlines the description of the parkland to be alienated by\nthe county of Nassau to Lakeside Inn, Inc. for residential improvements.\n\nSection 4 outlines the description of the land to be conveyed by Lake-\nside Inn, Inc. to the county of Nassau and dedicated as parkland.\n\nSection 5 provides that if the land acquired by the county of Nassau\nfrom section 4 should have a fair market value that is not equal to or\ngreater than the fair market value of the land alienated by\n\nSection 3, then the county of Nassau shall dedicate the difference of\nthe fair market value of the lands to be alienated and the lands to be\ndedicated for the acquisition of additional parklands and/or capital\nimprovements of existing parks and recreational facilities.\n\nSection 6 provides that if the county of Nassau has received any funding\nsupport or assistance from the federal government for the purchase,\nmaintenance, or improvement of the land outlined in section 3, this land\nshall not be discontinued and alienated until the county of Nassau has_\ncomplied with any federal requirements pertaining to the alienation or\nconversion of parklands, including satisfying all conditions that the\nsecretary of the interior deems necessary to assure the substitution of\nother lands shall be equivalent in fair market value and usefulness of\nthe land being alienated or converted.\n\nSection 7 contains the enacting clause.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation transfers ownership of parts of Milburn Pond Park from\nthe county of Nassau to the Lakeside Inn, Inc. for the purpose of resi-\ndential improvements. Through these residential improvements, Lakeside\nInn, Inc. would be able to make necessary modifications to expand their\nCoral House venue in the Town of Baldwin. With this expansion, Lakeside\nInn, Inc. will also convey land back to the county of Nassau for the\nMilburn'Pond Park. This expansion of the Coral Restaurant would allow\nmore local employment opportunities and further encourage local business\ndevelopment and local engagement within the county of Nassau.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately after it shall have become law.\n",
